1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+4{t}^{2}+2} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-2{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)-4}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{t}^{2}}+2L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{{x}_{2}(t)}-4L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L{{t}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\n$$\n\n we can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{8}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382967 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca890a8e-9ddd-51f7-9784-c9c1f020adef" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59740fa8-f90c-5914-9828-9748851bf279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382969} {:answer/id #uuid "87bb26d1-e423-5e9f-a59d-398ca721a2bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382970} {:answer/id #uuid "971a3190-698e-5a53-93e1-e6d27cf6faa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382971} {:answer/id #uuid "787ca528-afe2-556d-9b29-dc0c2920b9ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382972