{X}_{1}(s)={{field-1}} \\\\ {{field-2}}=-3{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)+{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+6} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+6L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{{x}_{2}(t)}+L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the result\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s},\n$$\n\n we can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=-3{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca890a8e-9ddd-51f7-9784-c9c1f020adef" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01cbac4a-2654-5f98-9241-b446b05d72f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383001} {:answer/id #uuid "a942c037-e1a7-5590-955c-663483bf9c8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383002} {:answer/id #uuid "fcec4b52-0bb3-57cb-bd54-ed35d81db02b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383003} {:answer/id #uuid "b80ea7bd-e565-5d92-8100-a82d25e9720c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01cbac4a-2654-5f98-9241-b446b05d72f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383001} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3a27ada-79a4-5684-8e4a-89ec893dfe52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "351c1713-b816-5c13-bc80-35ed02095511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383006} {:answer/id #uuid "608d805e-a746-55f7-ad20-4c41841028d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383007} {:answer/id #uuid "4afe31a0-83d1-5a3d-8f67-0c2ee3c2a4fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383008} {:answer/id #uuid "7085decd-b020-5492-bae5-dce2447e141b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4afe31a0-83d1-5a3d-8f67-0c2ee3c2a4fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383008} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d8bd303-0b44-52c0-9d11-1f5b68ff3997" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a895298-e7e5-50a5-974c-4bda1e925a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383011} {:answer/id #uuid "5eefe84c-8057-55bd-88a7-fd975739439c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383012} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5e8459-2dfb-5042-9df3-d39d3784093c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383013} {:answer/id #uuid "636cb5f3-1400-5710-b537-417f00e02a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5eefe84c-8057-55bd-88a7-fd975739439c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383012} :answer-field/id #uuid "abbf0a57-7427-5b8a-8f53-4009cd7c0740" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d13bb8d6-abdb-56b1-aa9c-35123b36b876" :question/math-academy-id "q-332825" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)-1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}={{field-2}} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)-{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)-1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+3L{{x}_{2}(t)}-L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+9} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3259fb49-8b62-5e7c-814c-5ccf996446b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-s^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383015} {:answer/id #uuid "952c48d0-e090-5c39-8ce5-360fe6a233ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3259fb49-8b62-5e7c-814c-5ccf996446b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-s^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383015} :answer-field/id #uuid "d908a6ad-bb07-5b6f-b150-d8b540c4eaef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "968c34ea-6536-56be-a722-82e75e44e26e" :question/math-academy-id "q-333064" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t)+4,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{3{x}_{2}(t)+4}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L{{x}_{2}(t)}+4L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =2+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & ={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =2{X}_{2}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =2(\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)})-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8}{s(s-3)}-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8-s(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8-{s}^{2}+3s}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc960939-7466-5837-a3c8-8c2d9ec61bff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc960939-7466-5837-a3c8-8c2d9ec61bff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383019} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b249152-cd1c-5fa5-b2d9-815f8901e0be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e9610af-8627-5644-9e8a-233c67193c2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-333070" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{5{x}_{2}(t)+2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+3L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=5L{{x}_{2}(t)}+2L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-0=2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=5{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =5{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =1+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3(\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}) \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-5)(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c90d6e72-1ef3-5a08-ab22-e39cf04b4ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s^{2}-7s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383022} {:answer/id #uuid "814838a9-e8b0-563c-86d9-7b7c56ae3169" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "814838a9-e8b0-563c-86d9-7b7c56ae3169" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383023} :answer-field/id #uuid "195c2464-955c-5cf0-92f5-d81c249bcaef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "651a9779-f6de-5b80-8654-32c2c2209844" :question/math-academy-id "q-333071" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{2}(t)+6,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{4{x}_{2}(t)+6}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=4L{{x}_{2}(t)}+6L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=-3{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{6}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{6}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-1+\\frac{6}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-s+6}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =-3{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =2+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =2+(\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s(s-4)+6-s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}-4s)+6-s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-8s+6-s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be2015f-fdf1-586e-a915-01a2d0eeff2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2be2015f-fdf1-586e-a915-01a2d0eeff2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383026} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2543f78-09cc-5180-a989-4e295efa12f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "814d05ba-3fb8-5518-a28e-318cafedbdd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-333073" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{3{x}_{2}(t)+1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=4L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L{{x}_{2}(t)}+L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=4{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =2+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+1}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =4{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =1+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =1+(\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s(s-3)+2s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-3s+2s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "310efa2f-7faf-5920-8172-91c6fd787af6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-t}+3e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383029} {:answer/id #uuid "4f95e8f1-4539-5c94-8b5c-40e24f950755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t}+3e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "310efa2f-7faf-5920-8172-91c6fd787af6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-t}+3e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383029} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b71c073-9ac4-5ea6-b889-00e23e40dd27" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383028} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92899a09-df9c-5618-8a98-b0e415f3a535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92899a09-df9c-5618-8a98-b0e415f3a535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383032} :answer-field/id #uuid "1440bfec-292d-5009-bf1a-a3098f3c4fd1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4af00dc3-1f8e-5a70-8450-3daf7f891fed" :question/math-academy-id "q-333133" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)+9 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}+3{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}+3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e225d997-4bc4-5783-a5cb-3e279053bf13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{t}+e^{2t}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e225d997-4bc4-5783-a5cb-3e279053bf13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{t}+e^{2t}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383035} :answer-field/id #uuid "67691548-2460-5ba8-a5ea-acc942e9ce8a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383034} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5b60664-c27a-5a0f-9f6e-bd7366469b72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5b60664-c27a-5a0f-9f6e-bd7366469b72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383037} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea061647-74da-5692-843a-8b2a00368435" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81391d77-04a8-59d4-9606-6ad64873b99c" :question/math-academy-id "q-333134" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{1\\cdot t}+{e}^{2\\cdot t}-2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ad689f9-693a-5e23-bbf7-4914ad26c689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{-2t}+3e^{t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ad689f9-693a-5e23-bbf7-4914ad26c689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{-2t}+3e^{t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383040} :answer-field/id #uuid "10ed8289-1747-5826-a3e7-724e9df91a76" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "789cf4dc-69d3-5290-acda-23900396e1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "789cf4dc-69d3-5290-acda-23900396e1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383042} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d01d122-8cbd-5a2c-b84e-f710648a0858" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b23ad7d-d82f-515a-9af4-4e7a337b8a30" :question/math-academy-id "q-333137" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)-20 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)-2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{2}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\cdot t}+3{e}^{1\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}+2 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a351b36-7df6-5c3e-b421-2d95db069374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e^{-t}+e^{2t}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a351b36-7df6-5c3e-b421-2d95db069374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e^{-t}+e^{2t}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383045} :answer-field/id #uuid "4de10fb4-0149-5d55-8c06-47fdedc53f90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6bbce55-b4fa-5bff-a3d6-c1b20adb3449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6bbce55-b4fa-5bff-a3d6-c1b20adb3449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383047} :answer-field/id #uuid "c742fa95-6e63-5b34-a291-ffcbe7f6f572" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ce4553dc-a6b5-5c6c-a88c-0467c4bf99b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-333138" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{2}(t)-1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=-\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-1\\cdot t}+{e}^{2\\cdot t}+2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =-1+{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ -1+{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
